Bellfruit are a pear-like type of fruit. Known for its musical properties, the tree produces spherical shells that emit melodious sounds when swayed in the wind.

They are sweet like peaches and have a unique shell. When the fruit is plucked or falls out it leaves a bell-like shell which makes sound in the wind. Wild Bellfruit is said to be even better and sweeter than the domesticated variants.

The tree are able to grow in several places, but it is revered in the [[vianis-river-delta|Vianis River Delta]]. One of the oldest Bellfruit tree stands in [[romanikha|Romanikha]]

